### 1. Sketch the decision matrix  
| Criterion | Interface | Abstract class |
|-----------|-----------|----------------|
| Multiple inheritance | ✔︎ (a class can implement many interfaces) | ✘ (single inheritance only) |
| Shared implementation | ✘ (no code, only signatures) | ✔︎ (can provide concrete methods, fields) |
| Versioning | ❓ (adding a method breaks all implementers) | ✔︎ (new default methods can be added without breaking) |
| Conceptual role | “What can it do?” (behaviour contract) | “What is it?” (partial type hierarchy) |
| Need for state | ✘ (no fields, only constants) | ✔︎ (protected fields, constructors) |

